<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0043/tu_0008> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "When congestion fails to improve in response to diuretic therapy, the following options should be considered: • Re-evaluating presence/absence of congestion • Sodium and fluid restriction, • Increasing doses of loop diuretic, • Continuous infusion of a loop diuretic, or • Addition of a second type of diuretic orally (metolazone or spironolactone) or intravenously (chlorothiazide). Another option, ultrafiltration, may be considered. (Strength of Evidence = C)" .
