<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0043/e_0028/normalization> <http://digistrucmed.org/normalizationMappingStatus> "UNMAPPED" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0043/e_0071> <http://digistrucmed.org/charEnd> "156"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0043/tu_0010> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasSourceGradeRecord> <http://digistrucmed.org/grade-record/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0043/gr_0015> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0043/tu_0002> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "It is recommended that diuretics be administered at doses needed to produce a rate of diuresis sufficient to achieve optimal volume status with relief of signs and symptoms of congestion (edema, elevated JVP, dyspnea), without inducing an excessively rapid reduction in 1) intravascular volume, which may result in symptomatic hypotension and/or worsening renal function, or 2) serum electrolytes, which may precipitate arrhythmias or muscle cramps. (Strength of Evidence = C)" .
